# Corpus artifacts: what is tracked here mirrors what was tracked before the
# per-corpus restructure -- moving files must not silently change git's contents.
#
# The ECHR trees are the tree-depth ablation sweep. They lived in
# tree_depth_ablation/trees/, which ignored them as "generated per-config and
# rebuildable", and they stay ignored here. Everything else a corpus needs
# (chunks.json, chunks_with_embeddings.json, manifest.json) stays tracked, so a
# fresh clone can rebuild any ignored tree with:
#
#     python build_tree.py --dataset ECHR --subset convention \
#         --tree-version bottom-up-mc10 --max-children 10 --llm <model>
#
ECHR/convention/trees/*.pkl
ECHR/convention/trees/*.json
ECHR/convention/trees/summary_cache_*.json
